{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791820546,"nonce":"2TACTK2WB6CFG2Hai9cRU1EfHBw=","title":"A3 matching hardening before A5 (PR 175 re-review)","message":"Fix before A5 auto-recording: 1) fragments other than #/ and #! (e.g. #job=111, #jobs/111, #4567) are dropped by normalization but still decide; a fragment with a digit, = or / should never decide. Also: 2) weak id tokens (any *_id param, all-digit path segments like /page/2 or Taleo careersection/2, any 4-digit run like years and ZIPs) let list pages count as one posting; 3) redirect params (u, r, url, target, redirect) honoured on any host so a back-link decides; restrict to known redirector hosts; 4) stripped tracking params that are the job id (ref, source, src, mode, trk) collapse jobs; 5) N8: Referral, Employee referral, Referred by, Referrer sections should block own contact; 6) A5 note: a generic session open on a no-id list URL binds other jobs' modals in the same tab via rule 1. Usability: count UUIDs or 16+ hex runs as ids (166 of 203 real asks are NLX GUIDs and hire.wyo.gov ObjectIds).","files":null}]}